/P 302 0 R
/ActualText (Statistics and probability are essential for data analysis because they help us understand and make sense of data. Statistics allows us to summarize large amounts of information using numbers like averages and ranges, so we can see patterns and trends. Probability helps us predict future events and understand the likelihood of different outcomes. Together, they provide the tools we need to turn raw data into useful insights. This is important for making informed decisions and solving real-world problems. Learning statistics and probability is crucial for anyone who wants to work with data and make data-driven decisions.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
